{"id":"multiprocessing/RLock.release","module":"multiprocessing","qualname":"RLock.release","name":"release","kind":"method","parent":"multiprocessing/RLock","signatures":["RLock.release()"],"doc":"Release a lock, decrementing the recursion level. If after the decrement the recursion level is zero, reset the lock to unlocked (not owned by any process or thread) and if any other processes or threads are blocked waiting for the lock to become unlocked, allow exactly one of them to proceed. If after the decrement the recursion level is still nonzero, the lock remains locked and owned by the calling process or thread.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/multiprocessing.html#multiprocessing.RLock.release","added":null,"changed":[],"deprecated":null,"availability":["not Android","not iOS","not WASI"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
